config FIBRIL_CAN_NODE_MD_MOTOR
	bool
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_FIBRIL_FCAN_MD_MOTOR_ENABLED
	select MOTOR
	select ENCODER
	select MOTOR_CONTROL
	help
	  Compiled whenever the devicetree pairs motors with encoders under a
	  fibril,fcan-md-motor node, which is also what puts MdMotor instances
	  into the schema.

	  The leaf drivers are not selected here: they are on by default once
	  their own devicetree nodes exist, and this function works with any
	  motor and encoder class device.

config FIBRIL_CAN_NODE_MD_MOTOR_MAX
	int "MdMotor instances to allocate for"
	default 8
	range 1 32
	depends on FIBRIL_CAN_NODE_MD_MOTOR
	help
	  The schema's max_count for MdMotor: how many instances the generated
	  code reserves state for. It is a ceiling, not a count, and never
	  reaches the schema blob.

	  8 covers every RoboMaster a two-bus board can address, which is the
	  most CanMotorMbed ever drove from one board. Lowering it below the
	  devicetree's length fails the BUILD_ASSERT in md_motor.cpp.
